\ Phase 4 slice 6a: the polymorphic array combinators, written in Sooth and
\ inlined (term-spliced) at every concrete call site, so each lowers to a tight
\ `times` loop with no per-element call and runs in constant stack.
\
\ Each is a leaf combinator: it drives a `times` loop directly and hands one
\ element to its quotation parameter per iteration. `map`/`fold` are NOT built
\ on `each`, but this is a cost choice, not an impossibility: `fold` over `each`
\ is expressible by riding the accumulator in a captured one-element array
\ reached by balanced `&`/`&!` borrows inside the literal (D3 accepts balanced
\ borrows), and `map` likewise with a second captured counter cell for the
\ index. The reason to keep them leaves is that inlining is total: a quotation
\ has no runtime representation, so splicing is the only lowering, and library
\ composition depth is code size at every call site. Building `map` on `each`
\ would make every `map` call site depth 2 and cost an extra array copy and a
\ counter cell; a leaf keeps the library flat at depth 1. They share the loop
\ shape, not a call.

export: each map fold filter while ;

: each ( ['T 'N] [ 'T -- ] -- )
  | f | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  count [ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call ] times
  arr drop ;

: map ( ['T 'N] [ 'T -- 'T ] -- ['T 'N] )
  | f | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  count [ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call | v | &!arr i >usize &!> v ! ] times
  arr ;

: fold ( ['T 'N] 'A [ 'A 'T -- 'A ] -- 'A )
  | f | | acc | len >i64 | count | | arr |
  acc count [ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ f call ] times
  arr drop ;

\ `filter` compacts an array in place, keeping only the elements for which the
\ predicate returns true. The write cursor `w` threads on the stack below the
\ `times` index, exactly as `fold` threads its accumulator: it must not be
\ rebound inside the body (a rebind is a fresh per-iteration local and `times`
\ forbids carrying move-state across the back-edge). `'T: Copy` is declared
\ because the body `dup`s the element; no non-`Copy`-element array can be
\ built today (`fill` rejects a linear element), so the bound is currently
\ inert but honest.
: filter ( ['T: Copy 'N] [ 'T -- bool ] -- ['T 'N] usize )
  | p | len >i64 | n | | arr |
  0 n [ | i | &arr i >usize &> @ dup p call if
          | v | &!arr over >usize &!> v ! 1 +
        else drop end ] times
  | wf | arr wf >usize ;

\ `while` threads a state `'a` through its predicate until the predicate
\ returns false, then leaves the state. It is a self-*tail* combinator: the
\ recursive `p while` in tail position lowers to a loop back-edge (D8), not an
\ endless splice, so `while` runs in constant stack. The self-edge is the only
\ recursion 6b's relaxed cycle check (D5) admits; the quotation `p` is `Copy`
\ and re-resolved statically each iteration, carried in no loop phi.
: while ( 'a [ 'a -- 'a bool ] -- 'a )
  | p | p call if p while else end ;
